WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.515
Here's the problem in one sentence:
a token can prove who signed a claim,

2
00:00:04.515 --> 00:00:06.787
but not that the claim is still true.

3
00:00:06.787 --> 00:00:09.675
The timeline shows how an
orphaned account happens.

4
00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:14.159
HR knows about a separation two weeks
early, and nothing else is listening,

5
00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:18.863
so the last forgotten account turns up
in a penetration test six months later.

6
00:00:18.863 --> 00:00:22.038
Nobody was careless;
there was simply no wire.

7
00:00:22.038 --> 00:00:23.526
And the cost has gone up.

8
00:00:23.526 --> 00:00:29.139
Under Zero Trust, access is decided per
session from attributes and dynamic groups,

9
00:00:29.139 --> 00:00:32.638
so a wrong department isn't
a phone-book typo any more.

10
00:00:32.638 --> 00:00:33.938
It's wrong access.

11
00:00:33.938 --> 00:00:37.010
Next, the architecture
that fixes the wiring.
